# What reaches the Vercel build host, from the repository root.
#
# `apps/web/.vercelignore` only applies when the Vercel project's Root
# Directory is set to `apps/web`. When it is the repository root - the default,
# and what this project is on - that file is never read, so the exclusions have
# to exist here too.
#
# `.env` is gitignored, so it cannot arrive through git. But `vercel deploy`
# from a working copy uploads the *directory*, not the commit. This is the
# second lock on the same door (`CLAUDE.md`: "Secrets never enter the repo").
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# The API is not a client asset, and it is the half of the repository that
# holds the résumé pipeline, the AI layer and the database models. None of it
# belongs on a static-hosting build host.
apps/api

# The specification and the tooling are not client assets either. `docs/spec/`
# in particular is 20 files of product decisions on a public host.
docs
infra
packages

node_modules
apps/web/node_modules
apps/web/dist
.vite
.venv

# Build caches and local artifacts.
__pycache__
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
.mypy_cache
